mokratis has hexproof unless it's attacking or blocking.\\nTromokratis can't be blocked unless all creatures defending player controls block it. (If any creature that player controls doesn't block this creature, it can't be blocked.)", 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nDestroy all creatures.', 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nDestroy two target creatures.', 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nExile two target creatures. For each of those creatures, its controller reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a creature card, puts that card onto the battlefield, then shuffles the rest into their library.', 'Undergrowth Stadium enters the battlefield tapped unless you have two or more opponents.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Undergrowth — When Lotleth Giant enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to target opponent for each creature card in your graveyard.', "Untap Endbringer during each other player's untap step.\\n{T}: Endbringer deals 1 damage to any target.\\n{C}, {T}: Target creature can't attack or block this turn.\\n{C}{C}, {T}: Draw a card.", 'Untap all creatures and gain control of them until end of turn. They gain haste until end of turn.', 'Until end of turn, target creature gets +2/+0 and gains "When this creature dies, return it to the battlefield tapped under its owner\'s control."', 'Vault of Champions enters the battlefield tapped unless you have two or more opponents.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)\\nReach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)", 'Vigilance, reach, trample\\nWhen Zacama, Primal Calamity enters the battlefield, if you cast it, untap all lands you control.\\n{2}{R}: Zacama deals 3 damage to target creature.\\n{2}{G}: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n{2}{W}: You gain 3 life.', 'Vigilance, trample\\nIf one or more +1/+1 counters would be put on Mowu, Loyal Companion, that many plus one +1/+1 counters are put on it instead.', "Vigilance\\nCreatures can't attack you or planeswalkers you control unless their controller pays {1} for each of those creatures.", 'Vigilance\\nLieutenant — At the beginning of combat on your turn, if you control your commander, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to creatures you control this turn. Other creatures you control gain vigilance until end of turn.', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Staunch Throneguard enters the battlefield, you become the monarch.', "Vigilance\\n{1}, {T}: Copy target activated or triggered ability you control from a colorless source. You may choose new targets for the copy. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", 'Vigilance\\n{2}{W}, {T}: Create a 2/2 white Knight creature token with vigilance.\\n{B}, {T}, Tap X untapped Knights you control: Destroy target creature with power X or less.', 'When Alharu, Solemn Ritualist enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two other target creatures.\\nWhenever a nontoken creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)', 'When Ancestral Blade enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token, then attach Ancestral Blade to it.\\nEquipped creature gets +1/+1.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'When Armorcraft Judge enters the battlefield, draw a card for each creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'When Bastion of Remembrance enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.\\nWhenever a creature you control dies, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', "When Brinelin, the Moon Kraken enters the battlefield or whenever you cast a spell with mana value 6 or greater, you may return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)", "When Cacophony Unleashed enters the battlefield, if you cast it, destroy all nonenchantment creatures.\\nWhenever Cacophony Unleashed or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, until end of turn, Cacophony Unleashed becomes a legendary 6/6 Nightmare God creature with menace and deathtouch. It's still an enchantment.", 'When Carrier Thrall dies, create a 1/1 colorless Eldrazi Scion creature token. It has "Sacrifice this creature: Add {C}."', "When Corpse Augur dies, you draw X cards and you lose X life, where X is the number of creature cards in target player's graveyard.", 'When Cyclops Electromancer enters the battlefield, it deals X damage to target creature an opponent controls, where X is the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.', 'When Deepglow Skate enters the battlefield, double the number of each kind of counter on any number of target permanents.', "When Demon's Disciple enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature or planeswalker.", 'When Dread Drone enters the battlefield, create two 0/1 colorless Eldrazi Spawn creature tokens. They have "Sacrifice this creature: Add {C}."', 'When Dwarven Hammer enters the battlefield, you may pay {2}. If you do, create a 2/1 red Dwarf Berserker creature token, then attach Dwarven Hammer to it.\\nEquipped creature gets +3/+0 and has trample.\\nEquip {3}', 'When Elite Scaleguard enters the battlefield, bolster 2. (Choose a creature with the least toughness among creatures you control and put two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nWhenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it attacks, tap target creature defending player controls.', "When Entourage of Trest enters the battlefield, you become the monarch.\\nEntourage of Trest can block an additional creature each combat as long as you're the monarch.", 'When Eternal Witness enters the battlefield, you may return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Fierce Empath enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a creature card with mana value 6 or greater, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Gavony Silversmith enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.', 'When Godo, Bandit Warlord enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Equipment card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\nWhenever Godo attacks for the first time each turn, untap it and all Samurai you control. After this phase, there is an additional combat phase.', "When Grasp of Fate enters the battlefield, for each opponent, exile up to one target nonland permanent that player controls until Grasp of Fate leaves the battlefield. (Those permanents return under their owners' control.)", 'When Impulsive Pilferer dies, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nEncore {3}{R} ({3}{R}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.)', 'When Inga Rune-Eyes enters the battlefield, scry 3.\\nWhen Inga Rune-Eyes dies, draw three cards if three or more creatures died this turn.', 'When Kaho, Minamo Historian enters the battlefield, search your library for up to three instant cards, exile them, then shuffle.\\n{X}, {T}: You may cast a spell with mana value X from among cards exiled with Kaho without paying its mana cost.', 'When Kozilek\'s Predator enters the battlefield, create two 0/1 colorless Eldrazi Spawn creature tokens. They have "Sacrifice this creature: Add {C}."', 'When Living Lightning dies, return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Meteor Golem enters the battlefield, destroy target nonland permanent an opponent controls.', 'When Myr Sire dies, create a 1/1 colorless Phyrexian Myr artifact creature token.', 'When Oath of Gideon enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 white Kor Ally creature tokens.\\nEach planeswalker you control enters the battlefield with an additional loyalty counter on it.', 'When Oath of Jace enters the battlefield, draw three cards, then discard two cards.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, scry X, where X is the number of planeswalkers you control.', "When Oath of Teferi enters the battlefield, exile another target permanent you control. Return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.\\nYou may activate the loyalty abilities of planeswalkers you control twice each turn rather than only once.", 'When Oreskos Explorer enters the battlefield, search your library for up to X Plains cards, where X is the number of players who control more lands than you. Reveal those cards, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Palace Jailer enters the battlefield, you become the monarch.\\nWhen Palace Jailer enters the battlefield, exile target creature an opponent controls until an opponent becomes the monarch.', 'When Palace Sentinels enters the battlefield, you become the monarch.', 'When Phyrexian Gargantua enters the battlefield, you draw two cards and you lose 2 life.', 'When Phyrexian Triniform dies, create three 3/3 colorless Phyrexian Golem artifact creature tokens.\\nEncore {12} ({12}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.)', 'When Pollenbright Druid enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n• Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', 'When Priest of the Blood Rite enters the battlefield, create a 5/5 black Demon creature token with flying.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 2 life.', 'When Prophetic Prism enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'When Rishkar, Peema Renegade enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.\\nEach creature you control with a counter on it has "{T}: Add {G}."', 'When Serrated Scorpion dies, it deals 2 damage to each opponent and you gain 2 life.', 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Spellseeker enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an instant or sorcery card with mana value 2 or less, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Spirited Companion enters the battlefield, draw a card.', "When Spitebellows leaves the battlefield, it deals 6 damage to target creature.\\nEvoke {1}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its evoke cost. If you do, it's sacrificed when it enters the battlefield.)", 'When Supply Runners enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control.', 'When Teyo, Geometric Tactician enters the battlefield, create a 0/4 white Wall creature token with defender and flying.\\n[+1]: You and target opponent each draw a card.\\n[−2]: Choose left or right. Until your next turn, each player may attack only the nearest opponent in the last chosen direction and planeswalkers controlled by that opponent.', 'When Thraben Inspector enters the battlefield, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'When Urza, Lord High Artificer enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 colorless Construct artifact creature token with "This creature gets +1/+1 for each artifact you control."\\nTap an untapped artifact you control: Add {U}.\\n{5}: Shuffle your library, then exile the top card. Until end of turn, you may play that card without paying its mana cost.', 'When Vindictive Lich dies, choose one or more. Each mode must target a different player.\\n• Target opponent sacrifices a creature.\\n• Target opponent discards two cards.\\n• Target opponent loses 5 life.', "When Wakening Sun's Avatar enters the battlefield, if you cast it from your hand, destroy all non-Dinosaur creatures.", "When Whirler Rogue enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.\\nTap two untapped artifacts you control: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'When Witching Well enters the battlefield, scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)\\n{3}{U}, Sacrifice Witching Well: Draw two cards.', 'When you cast this spell, copy it. (The copy becomes a token.)\\nEquipped creature has double strike as long as two or more Equipment are attached to it.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'When you cast this spell, exile two target permanents.\\nIndestructible\\nWhenever Ulamog, the Ceaseless Hunger attacks, defending player exiles the top twenty cards of their library.', 'When you cast this spell, gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. Until end of turn, it has base power and toughness 10/10, and gains trample, annihilator 2, and haste.\\nAnnihilator 2 (Whenever this creature attacks, defending player sacrifices two permanents.)\\nTrample', 'When you cast this spell, if you have fewer than seven cards in hand, draw cards equal to the difference.\\nMenace\\nDiscard a card with mana value X: Counter target spell with mana value X.', 'When you cast this spell, target opponent exiles the top four cards of their library, then you may put any number of land cards that player owns from exile onto the battlefield under your control.', 'When you cast this spell, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nAnnihilator 2 (Whenever this creature attacks, defending player sacrifices two permanents.)', 'When you next cast an instant spell, cast a sorcery spell, or activate a loyalty ability this turn, copy that spell or ability twice. You may choose new targets for the copies.', 'Whenever Bane of Bala Ged attacks, defending player exiles two permanents they control.', 'Whenever Hammer of Nazahn or another Equipment enters the battlefield under your control, you may attach that Equipment to target creature you control.\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+0 and has indestructible.\\nEquip {4}', "Whenever Lorthos, the Tidemaker attacks, you may pay {8}. If you do, tap up to eight target permanents. Those permanents don't untap during their controllers' next untap steps.", 'Whenever Pianna, Nomad Captain attacks, attacking creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Scaretiller becomes tapped, choose one —\\n• You may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.\\n• Return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', 'Whenever Sidisi, Brood Tyrant enters the battlefield or attacks, mill three cards.\\nWhenever one or more creature cards are put into your graveyard from your library, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', 'Whenever Tuya Bearclaw attacks, it gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the greatest power among other creatures you control.', 'Whenever a Saproling you control dies, Slimefoot, the Stowaway deals 1 damage to each opponent and you gain 1 life.\\n{4}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'Whenever a Sliver creature you control becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell or ability unless its controller pays {2}.', 'Whenever a Sliver deals combat damage to a player, its controller may create a 1/1 colorless Sliver creature token.', 'Whenever a Sliver deals combat damage to a player, its controller may draw a card.', 'Whenever a commander you control attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)', "Whenever a creature an opponent controls attacks, if you're the defending player, create a 3/3 red Ogre creature token unless that creature's controller pays {3}.", 'Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, each Dragon you control deals 1 damage to that creature.\\n[+1]: Until end of turn, each planeswalker you control becomes a 4/4 red Dragon creature and gains flying.\\n[−3]: Create a 4/4 red Dragon creature token with flying.', "Whenever a creature with power 1 or less is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may return that card to the battlefield at the beginning of the next end step if Shirei, Shizo's Caretaker is still on the battlefield.", "Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, add that much {G}. Until end of turn, you don't lose this mana as steps and phases end.", "Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, choose one —\\n• Goad target creature that player controls.\\n• Exile the top card of that player's library. Until end of turn, you may cast that card and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast that spell.", 'Whenever a creature you control dies, each other player sacrifices a creature.', 'Whenever a token you control leaves the battlefield, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever an Equipment enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card.\\nMetalcraft — Equipment you control have equip {0} as long as you control three or more artifacts.', "Whenever an enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, you may create a token that's a copy of it. Do this only once each turn.", "Whenever an opponent attacks you and/or one or more planeswalkers you control, exile the top card of that player's library. You may play that card for as long as it remains exiled, and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast it.", 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, that player may pay {2}. If the player doesn\'t, you create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'Whenever an opponent taps an artifact for mana, gain control of that artifact until the end of your next turn.', "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, its controller may draw a card if its power is greater than each other creature's power.\\n{G}, {T}: Add X mana in any combination of colors, where X is the greatest power among creatures you control.", 'Whenever another creature you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Rot Shambler.', "Whenever another creature you control dies, you get an experience counter.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, choose target creature card in your graveyard. If that card's mana value is less than or equal to the number of experience counters you have, return it to the battlefield. Otherwise, put it into your hand.", 'Whenever another nontoken creature dies, you may create a 1/1 black Rat creature token.\\nRats you control have deathtouch.', 'Whenever another nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, bolster 1. (Choose a creature with the least toughness among creatures you control and put a +1/+1 counter on it.)', 'Whenever another nontoken creature you control dies, create a 3/1 black and red Graveborn creature token with haste.', "Whenever another nontoken creature you control dies, you may return it to the battlefield face down under its owner's control. It's a Forest land. (It has no other types or abilities.)", 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, Heart-Piercer Bow deals 1 damage to target creature defending player controls.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Whenever equipped creature attacks, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield tapped.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Whenever one or more creatures attack one of your opponents or a planeswalker they control, those creatures gain menace until end of turn.', 'Whenever one or more creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, you may sacrifice one of them. If you do, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card that shares a creature type with the sacrificed creature. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'Whenever you attack a player with one or more equipped creatures, draw a card.\\n{W}: You may unattach an Equipment from a creature you control. If you do, tap that creature and it gains indestructible until end of turn.', "Whenever you cast a colorless creature spell, manifest the top card of your library. (Put it onto the battlefield face down as a 2/2 creature. Turn it face up any time for its mana cost if it's a creature card.)\\nWhenever you attack with creatures with total power 6 or greater, you may turn a face-down creature you control face up.", "Whenever you cast a creature spell, create X 1/1 black Thrull creature tokens, where X is that spell's mana value.\\nWhen you control seven or more Thrulls, sacrifice Endrek Sahr, Master Breeder.", "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.\\n[−2]: Target artifact you control becomes a copy of another target artifact or creature you control until end of turn, except it's an artifact in addition to its other types.", 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', 'Whenever you cast a planeswalker spell, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add two mana of different colors. Spend this mana only to cast planeswalker spells.', 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.\\n{1}{U}, Sacrifice two artifacts: Draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, create a 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature token.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you gain 1 life and draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell that targets only Zada, Hedron Grinder, copy that spell for each other creature you control that the spell could target. Each copy targets a different one of those creatures.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell with mana value greater than the number of experience counters you have, you get an experience counter.\\nInstant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less to cast for each experience counter you have.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 blue Bird Illusion creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 2/2 blue Drake creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast your third spell each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Captain Ripley Vance, then it deals damage equal to its power to any target.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 2/2 green Cat creature token.\\n{4}{G}{G}: Until end of turn, creatures you control have base power and toughness X/X, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Whenever you sacrifice a permanent, Havoc Jester deals 1 damage to any target.', "Whenever you sacrifice a permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on Blood Aspirant.\\n{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature or enchantment: Blood Aspirant deals 1 damage to target creature. That creature can't block this turn.", 'White spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'Wildwood Scourge enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever one or more +1/+1 counters are put on another non-Hydra creature you control, put a +1/+1 counter on Wildwood Scourge.', 'Worn Powerstone enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', "Xantcha, Sleeper Agent enters the battlefield under the control of an opponent of your choice.\\nXantcha attacks each combat if able and can't attack its owner or planeswalkers its owner controls.\\n{3}: Xantcha's controller loses 2 life and you draw a card. Any player may activate this ability.", "You don't lose unspent green mana as steps and phases end.\\nOmnath, Locus of Mana gets +1/+1 for each unspent green mana you have.", 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "You may exile two blue cards from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nGain control of target noncreature spell. You may choose new targets for it. (If that spell is an artifact, enchantment, or planeswalker, the permanent enters the battlefield under your control.)", 'You may have Body Double enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature card in a graveyard.', "You may have Spark Double enter the battlefield as a copy of a creature or planeswalker you control, except it enters with an additional +1/+1 counter on it if it's a creature, it enters with an additional loyalty counter on it if it's a planeswalker, and it isn't legendary.", 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may cast artifact spells and colorless spells from the top of your library.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Exile the top card of your library.', "You may pay {3}{U} and tap an untapped artifact you control rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nFlying", 'You may pay {W} and tap four untapped creatures you control with flying rather than pay this spell\'s mana cost.\\nFlying, lifelink\\nOther creatures you control with flying have indestructible. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy them.)', 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.\\nLands you control are every basic land type in addition to their other types.', 'You may play two additional lands on each of your turns.', '[+1]: Create three 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.\\n[−3]: Destroy all creatures with power 4 or greater.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +2/+2 and have flying."', '[+1]: Exile the top card of your library. You may cast that card. If you don\'t, Chandra, Torch of Defiance deals 2 damage to each opponent.\\n[+1]: Add {R}{R}.\\n[−3]: Chandra, Torch of Defiance deals 4 damage to target creature.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you cast a spell, this emblem deals 5 damage to any target."', "[+1]: Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal an enchantment card from among them and put that card into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−3]: Exile target creature or enchantment you don't control until target enchantment you control leaves the battlefield.\\n[−7]: Return all enchantment cards from your graveyard to the battlefield.", '[+1]: Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library.\\n[−1]: Untap up to four target permanents.\\n[−10]: You get an emblem with "You may activate loyalty abilities of planeswalkers you control on any player\'s turn any time you could cast an instant."\\nTeferi, Temporal Archmage can be your commander.', '[+1]: Until end of turn, up to one target creature gets +1/+1 and gains first strike, vigilance, and lifelink.\\n[−2]: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control and a loyalty counter on each other planeswalker you control.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "If a source would deal damage to you or a planeswalker you control, prevent all but 1 of that damage."', "[+1]: Until your next turn, whenever a creature an opponent controls attacks, it gets -1/-0 until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Reveal the top three cards of your library. An opponent separates those cards into two piles. Put one pile into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n[−8]: For each player, search that player's library for a nonland card and exile it, then that player shuffles. You may cast those cards without paying their mana costs.", '[+1]: Up to two other target planeswalkers you control phase out at the beginning of the next end step. (Treat them and anything attached to them as though they don\'t exist until your next turn.)\\n[−2]: For each opponent, return up to one target nonland permanent that player controls to its owner\'s hand.\\n[−7]: Target artifact you control becomes a 9/9 Construct artifact creature and gains vigilance, indestructible, and "This creature can\'t be blocked."', '[+1]: You gain 2 life. Add {U}, {R}, or {W}. Spend this mana only to cast a noncreature spell.\\n[−2]: Draw a card, then you may discard a card. When you discard a nonland card this way, Narset of the Ancient Way deals damage equal to that card\'s mana value to target creature or planeswalker.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this emblem deals 2 damage to any target."', '[+2]: Create a 1/1 green Elf Druid creature token with "{T}: Add {G}."\\n[−2]: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n[−6]: Draw a card for each green creature you control.\\nFreyalise, Llanowar\'s Fury can be your commander.', '[+2]: Create a 1/1 white Kor Soldier creature token. You may attach an Equipment you control to it.\\n[−2]: You may put an Equipment card from your hand or graveyard onto the battlefield.\\n[−10]: Create a colorless Equipment artifact token named Stoneforged Blade. It has indestructible, "Equipped creature gets +5/+5 and has double strike," and equip {0}.\\nNahiri, the Lithomancer can be your commander.', '[+2]: Discard up to two cards, then draw that many cards.\\n[−2]: Sacrifice an artifact. If you do, return target artifact card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n[−10]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an artifact is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield at the beginning of the next end step."\\nDaretti, Scrap Savant can be your commander.', "[+2]: During target opponent's next turn, creatures that player controls attack Gideon Jura if able.\\n[−2]: Destroy target tapped creature.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Gideon Jura becomes a 6/6 Human Soldier creature that's still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.", '[+2]: Each opponent loses 1 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.\\n[−2]: Create a 5/5 black Demon creature token with flying. You lose 2 life.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "{1}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain X life and draw X cards, where X is the sacrificed creature\'s power."\\nOb Nixilis of the Black Oath can be your commander.', '[+2]: Each player draws a card.\\n[−1]: Target player draws a card.\\n[−10]: Target player mills twenty cards.', '[+2]: You may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\\n[−2]: Exile target enchantment, tapped artifact, or tapped creature.\\n[−8]: Search your library for an artifact or creature card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. It gains haste. Return it to your hand at the beginning of the next end step.', '{1}, Sacrifice an artifact or creature: Makeshift Munitions deals 1 damage to any target.', "{1}, Sacrifice another creature: Legion Vanguard explores. (Reveal the top card of your library. Put that card into your hand if it's a land. Otherwise, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature, then put the card back or put it into your graveyard.)", '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: You gain 2 life.\\n{2}, {T}, Exile Campfire: Put all commanders you own from the command zone and from your graveyard into your hand. Then shuffle your graveyard into your library.', '{1}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life and draw a card.', '{1}{B}: Return Reassembling Skeleton from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', '{1}{G}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\nSacrifice two Saprolings: You gain 2 life and draw a card.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Font of Fertility: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Magus of the Wheel: Each player discards their hand, then draws seven cards.', '{1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Ashling the Pilgrim. If this is the third time this ability has resolved this turn, remove all +1/+1 counters from Ashling the Pilgrim, and it deals that much damage to each creature and each player.', '{1}{W}{U}, {T}: Return target artifact or enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Vial of Dragonfire: It deals 2 damage to target creature.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wayfarer's Bauble: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", '{2}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you control three or more lands with the same name.', '{2}: Mirage Mirror becomes a copy of target artifact, creature, enchantment, or land until end of turn.', '{2}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.\\n{2}{B}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', '{2}{G}, {T}, Put a verse counter on Yisan, the Wanderer Bard: Search your library for a creature card with mana value equal to the number of verse counters on Yisan, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{2}{G}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.\\n{4}{G}, {T}: Create an X/X colorless Construct artifact creature token, where X is the number of creatures you control.', '{2}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{2}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\nSacrifice a Saproling: Saproling creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{2}{U}, {T}: Each player mills three cards. Exile up to two creature cards put into graveyards this way. Create an X/X blue Zombie creature token, where X is the total power of the cards exiled this way.', '{2}{W}: Adapt 1. (If this creature has no +1/+1 counters on it, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhenever one or more +1/+1 counters are put on Knighted Myr, it gains double strike until end of turn.', '{3}, Sacrifice Burnished Hart: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{5}, {T}, Exile Perilous Vault: Exile all nonland permanents.', "{B}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature: Create X 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's power.", '{B}: Regenerate Twisted Abomination.\\nSwampcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Swamp card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{R}, {T}: Spikeshot Goblin deals damage equal to its power to any target.', '{R}: Inferno Titan gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nWhenever Inferno Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, it deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.', '{T}, Mill a card: Add {C}. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', '{T}, Put a page counter on Mazemind Tome: Scry 1.\\n{2}, {T}, Put a page counter on Mazemind Tome: Draw a card.\\nWhen there are four or more page counters on Mazemind Tome, exile it. If you do, you gain 4 life.', '{T}, Sacrifice Jeweled Lotus: Add three mana of any one color. Spend this mana only to cast your commander.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice two creatures: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{T}: Add X mana of any one color, where X is the number of enchantments you control.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color. If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, add two mana of any one color instead.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Letter of Acceptance: Draw a card.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{4}, {T}: Each player who controls a permanent named Bonder's Ornament draws a card.", '{T}: Add three mana of any one color.', '{T}: Add {C}.', '{T}: Add {C}. ({C} represents colorless mana.)\\n{2}{C}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you have no cards in hand.', "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Power-Plant, add {C}{C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Power-Plant and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nTap an untapped legendary permanent you control: Untap Honor-Worn Shaku.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity. If you spend this mana to cast your commander, it enters the battlefield with a number of additional +1/+1 counters on it equal to the number of times it's been cast from the command zone this game.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a storage counter on Mage-Ring Network.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Mage-Ring Network: Add {C} for each storage counter removed this way.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Until end of turn, creatures your opponents control lose hexproof and shroud and can't have hexproof or shroud.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Exile all graveyards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Each player draws a card, then discards a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Target legendary creature becomes a God in addition to its other types. Put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Tyrite Sanctum: Put an indestructible counter on target God.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: You gain 1 life for each colorless creature you control.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Pay life equal to the number of colors in your commanders' color identity: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}: Mobilized District becomes a 3/3 Citizen creature with vigilance until end of turn. It's still a land. This ability costs {1} less to activate for each legendary creature and planeswalker you control.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Unstable Obelisk: Destroy target permanent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R/W}, {T}: Add {R}{R}, {R}{W}, or {W}{W}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast colorless Eldrazi spells or activate abilities of colorless Eldrazi.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast colorless spells. Activate only if you control seven or more lands.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Talisman of Conviction deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Talisman of Creativity deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Talisman of Progress deals 1 damage to you.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Choose target commander that entered the battlefield this turn. Put a +1/+1 counter on it if it's a creature and a loyalty counter on it if it's a planeswalker.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{U/R}, {T}: Add {U}{U}, {U}{R}, or {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{W/U}, {T}: Add {W}{W}, {W}{U}, or {U}{U}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.\\n{U}, {T}: Search your library for a card named Heart-Piercer Bow or Vial of Dragonfire, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Hedron Archive: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Dreamstone Hedron: Draw three cards.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Choose a player. That player adds one mana of any color they choose.', '{T}: Create X 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens, where X is the number of Goblins you control.', '{T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you created a token this turn.\\n{8}, {T}, Sacrifice Idol of Oblivion: Create a 10/10 colorless Eldrazi creature token.', '{T}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, destroy all nonland permanents.', "{T}: Heartless Hidetsugu deals damage to each player equal to half that player's life total, rounded down.", '{T}: Untap another target permanent.\\nCycling {1}{U} ({1}{U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Vizier of Tumbling Sands, untap target permanent.']
flavor: ['"A blessing is not a gift. It is a duty."', '"A great many dangerous creatures call this region home. They all avoid the slivers."\\n—Foothill guide', '"A hedron holds magic for a thousand years—or less, if need be."', '"A life is meaningless until put to use."', '"A small sip here and a small sip there, and all of a sudden I need a new dance partner."', '"Aether is the soul of Kaladesh, and all souls should be free."', '"All are not equal—neither in life nor after death. Bontu\'s favorites will stand highest in eternity."\\n—Senifet, vizier of Bontu', '"All stories eventually come to an end."', '"Anyone can make their audience beg for an encore . . . I prefer mine to beg for mercy!"', '"Anyone who believes the elder dragons are the only ancient powers of this world has spent too much time listening to the elder dragons."\\n—Multani', '"Arise, great one, and cleanse the world of our enemies!"', '"As Yavimaya yearns to grow beyond its boundaries, so must we spend our lives seeking new horizons."', '"As my kha, he is the source of my inspiration. As my brother, he is the embodiment of my aspirations."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Be calm, wise spirit. You are in a world that is not your own, but I am not your enemy."', '"Beware the eager host."\\n—Eligeth, crossroads augur', '"Brago in his arrogance let the throne\'s defenses fall dormant. Our new queen is not so incautious."\\n—Livio, Oathsworn Sentinel', '"Brilliant! They evolved away from energy-taxing brains and respond only to spinal reflex arcs from the hive mind."\\n—Rukarumel, field journal', '"Captain, is now a good time to mention I\'m allergic to spiders?"', '"Captain, your units are the tip of our spear. There is zero room for failure."\\n—Jirina Kudro', '"Choices belong to those with the luxuries of time and distance. We have neither. I recommend we proceed with the plan to destroy all shrines of the kami."\\n—Lady Azami, letter to Sensei Hisoka', '"Come to slay the dragon for the good of the kingdom? How terribly predictable."', '"Dear brother, it\'s sweet that you have chosen to share your toys with Ludevic, but I too have found some new playmates."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Death tried to uncrown me. But now I return, king of a greater realm."', '"Die. But die knowing that your pathetic life will yield a great bounty for me."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Diplomacy has solved nothing. Only bloodspill can end this now. Call forth the warbringer."\\n—Basandra, Battle Seraph', '"Dissent will become perfection."\\n—Elesh Norn', '"Do the innocent pay for the crimes of the guilty? Of course they do. That\'s the fate of the weak."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"Does a serpent roar and chase its prey? No. A serpent waits silently for oblivious prey to draw near."', '"Does this choice really seem so simple, syr knight?"', '"Doves and pigeons are too subtle. When I send a message, I want it to have some teeth."\\n—Aeschel, royal diplomat', '"Even in death, we never stop growing."', '"Everything around here has cut a deal with gravity."\\n—Gerrard of the Weatherlight', '"Fate is not as fixed as you might think."', '"Fear holds no place in faith\'s battle plan."', '"Fire has always been my most faithful companion."\\n—Jared Carthalion', '"First you summon the lightning, then you make it dance."', '"Flowstone spreads, but new life spreads faster."', '"For justice and peace, I will keep watch."', '"For the lost and forgotten, I will keep watch."', '"For the sake of the Multiverse, I will keep watch."', '"For those without the Planeswalker spark, the merest touch of the Blind Eternities can kill."\\n—Ugin', '"Found families deserve a family crest too."\\n—Kinnan, bonder prodigy', '"Fuses? We have more than enough! Now . . . which one was it?"\\n—Flearan One-Eye, goblin engineer', '"Gaea knows what you need. Do you?"', '"Garl, adjust the slurry dispensers. Garl, fetch more corpses. Garl, quit crying and give me your brain tissue. If he doesn\'t stop being so rude, I\'m quitting."', '"Geralf, must you always whine? I agreed to nothing. I\'ll raise ghouls anytime I wish."', '"Go find yourself a couple of friends, and bring me a blindfold. Then we might have a fair fight."', '"Good ideas don\'t take time. They take a lot of bad ideas first."\\n—Ral Zarek', '"Graceful? Yes. Beautiful? Absolutely. Harmless? Definitely not."\\n—Fyndhorn elder', '"Grease up a firecannon good and proper with dinosaur-liver oil, and it\'ll shoot just about anything."', '"Have you ever held a Boros signet? There\'s a weight to it that belies its size—a weight of strength and of pride."\\n—Agrus Kos', '"He displays a perverse charisma fueled by avarice. Highly dangerous. Recommend civil sanctions."\\n—Agmand Sarv, Azorius hussar', '"His tenement is filled with the most vile, disgusting vermin. It\'s infested with rats, too."\\n—Branko One-Ear', '"Hold the line, for family and the fallen!"', '"Holy places are no longer sanctuary from death, and death is no longer sanctuary from anything."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"How truly vast this city must be, that I have traveled so far and seen so much, yet never once found the place where the buildings fail."', '"Humans bring nothing but suffering and deceit. They are not welcome in my forest."', '"Hunt somewhere else. This is your only warning."\\n—Gavi, nest warden', '"I am the bridge between sea and sky. Wind and waves alike rise at my whim."', '"I am who I pretend to be."', '"I await your donation."\\n—Dasha, Orzhov priest', '"I can\'t protect everyone here. But those I can, I will."\\n—Karn', '"I didn\'t say I would help you find your way home. I said I would help you finish your adventure."', '"I do as I please, little mortal. Do go on about your wishes, though—they amuse me to no end."', '"I do not miss Jukai Forest. It is not my home. My home is Kamigawa, its people my family. Wherever I set my pack and rest my head, I am home."', '"I don\'t have time for you right now."\\n—Teferi', '"I found a new toy. Wanna play?"', '"I hope the review board was paying attention, because my thesis would be hard to do twice."\\n—Spyracus, Prismari mage-student', '"I never thought I\'d spend my life fighting. I\'m a maker, not a destroyer."', '"I prefer the big and looming to the small and skittering."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"I stand with every member of my clan, and they stand with me."', '"I will protect the less fortunate. I will love bravely. I will face despair and fight on. As a Capashen, I can do no less."', '"I wish we\'d never visited that accursed hive. Even here, surrounded by nothing but clouds, I swear I can still hear the horrible clicking, slithering sounds."\\n—Monihan, aerial surveyor', '"I\'m not sure who\'s in charge around here, but I\'m pretty sure I know where to go to find out."\\n—Corliss the Wanderer', '"I\'ve heard enough from you, heretic."', '"I\'ve seen my share of baubles, minister. Whatever ostentatious bit of glitter you have there won\'t convince me to ... Oh my."\\n—Emperor Ayrelion', '"I\'ve survived a century\'s worth of assassination attempts, but this might be the most pathetic of them all."', '"If I die, feed me to a shambler. At least that way I\'ll be doing some good."\\n—Ryza, Oran-Rief scout', '"If they didn\'t want me to steal this, they should\'ve used more than seven layers of shatterproof antimagus glass."', '"If you travel only to reach a destination, you will miss the point of the journey."', '"If you work at sawing up carcasses, you notice how the joints fit, how the nerves are arrayed, and how the skin peels back."\\n—Ashnod, to Tawnos', '"If you\'ve been at this as long as I have, nothing can surprise you. That\'s the hope, at least."', '"Impress me."', '"Industry without artistry is just a fancy way to fill the junkyard."', '"Inform our allies in the Tenth and throw the circuit. It\'s about to get weird."', '"Inspiration is reciprocal: we all have a responsibility to each other to create."', '"Is the knowledge really forbidden because it is dangerous to you? Or perhaps because it is dangerous to those who seek to control you?"', '"It is possible that some queens are not born queens, but evolve into that form over time."\\n—Rukarumel, field notes', '"It is the fate of the weak to fall."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"It reflects the purity of Mirrodin-that-was."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"It seems docile enough. Perhaps we could train it to reap the grain—it would be the easiest harvest season of our lives!"\\n—Georgina, farmer, now deceased', '"It seems your ticket is in order after all, ma\'am."', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"It\'s a difficult task to quarantine a plague that moves with the clouds."\\n—Esara, healer adept', '"It\'s almost as exciting as watching a great battle from the Blood Age in person!"\\n—Quintorius, Lorehold mage-student', '"It\'s an ideal method for exploring sky ruins. The drakes sniff me briefly but then lose interest."', '"It\'s them or us."\\n—General Kudro', '"It\'s us against the world. Forever."', '"Just as new shoots rise from winter\'s slumber, so too will my people rise to greatness once again."', '"Kindly steer your fleet clear of the waters west of Scrub Isle. It would be a shame to incinerate such exquisite maritime craftsmanship."\\n—Commodore Axurik, to Admiral Yelise', '"Kinjalli\'s encompassing rays herald new life in the moment of the sun\'s dawning."\\n—Chitlati, Lightning Rider', '"Later we will mourn those we have lost. First we must end their suffering."\\n—Drana, Kalastria bloodchief', '"Leadership is both a blessing and a burden. Every day I strive to prove myself a worthy steward to those who follow me."', '"Life and death are two sides of the same coin."', '"Life grows everywhere. My kin merely find those places where it grows strongest."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"Linear time? You may as well believe in triangular gravity!"', '"Live an exemplary life. Die a worthy death. Rise in eternal glory."', '"Loneliness is a symptom of civilization."', '"Look how they beg for the knife! The Demonlord has trained them well."', '"Many thought they knew its weakness. They are dead."\\n—Kelsien, the Plague', '"Maybe they wanted to be on the winning side for once."\\n—Matoc, lavamancer', '"Mindless violence withers in the face of a master\'s skill."', '"Model? I\'m insulted. It\'s by all reasonable metrics a fully functional planetary system, scaled down for easier study."\\n—Urza, to Tawnos', '"My ancestor Toshiro used to say, \'Life is a series of choices between bad and worse.\' I\'m a master of making great bad choices."', '"My heart beats with the rhythm of the forest."', '"My mind is the spread of the canopy. My heart is the embrace of the roots. I am deathless Llanowar, its fury and its peace."', '"My time will come, when every soul will bask in my glory and obey my law."', '"My time will come, when no road will divide the endless verdure of the trees."', '"Need a medic! And some stonemasons!"\\n—Wyllon, Drannith merchant', '"Nice spell you got there. Be a shame if something happened to it."', '"Nine hells! How does something with no eyes see so far?"\\n—Max, Benalish scout', '"No angel bars our ascent. Emeria waits above!"', '"Nonsense! Everyone knows that snakes are sluggish and docile when cold!"\\n—Bodrick the Overconfident, last words', '"Of course it will grow beyond control—it was designed to choose its own evolution."\\n—Momir Vig', '"On vile wings and bloody wind, the swarm will rise."\\n—Skyclave inscription', '"Once I supply the breeze, you\'ll see your warriors for the smoke they truly are."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"One score and four he reigned, the Southland king: / A dragon coiled, a tiger poised below the mighty Yangtze."', '"One who ruled willing subjects would need no such protection."\\n—Adriana, Captain of the Guard', '"One would think I would be accustomed to unexpected returns."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"Only the weak imprison themselves behind walls. We live free under the wind, and our freedom makes us strong."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"Opposable thumbs, opposable toes, prehensile tails, boundary issues . . . no treasure is safe from a goblin."\\n—Captain Lannery Storm', '"Precise, clean cuts. No one saw anything. Again. Tag the report with my code and file it."\\n—Lavinia', '"Rich" is a relative term.', '"Scholars seek to understand the way the world is. I wish to shape the world into what it should be."', '"Send in your cavalry! Diaglu loves horsemeat."', '"Served cold? Nonsense! The best way to serve revenge is with an elephant of nervous disposition! Everyone knows that."\\n—Avenir the Petty', '"Since the last sliver arrived, even our mightiest relics splinter into shards as soon as we bring them against the hive."\\n—Llanach, Skyshroud ranger', '"Slaughter the weak ones. They are unworthy of the gift of *compleation.*"', '"Sleep now, brother. That is the one gift I can give you."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Slimefoot, I know I said I wanted to grow our repository of knowledge, but this isn\'t what I had in mind."', '"Some goblins are expendable. Some are impossible to get rid of. But he\'s both—at the same time!"\\n—Starke', '"Someone\'s been tampering with the graves again. But what kind of grave robber uses a pickax?"\\n—Morgan, cemetery groundskeeper', '"Sometimes you just need to be inspired by a massive explosion or a color that didn\'t exist five seconds ago."\\n—Rootha, Prismari mage-student', '"Species XR17 feeds upon the mental energies of its victims. This explains why the goblins remain unaffected."\\n—Riptide Project researcher', '"Spread out, you idiots! Spread out!"\\n—Marsden, party leader, last words', '"Sure, true self-worth has to come from within, but trophies are nice too."\\n—Killian, Silverquill mage-student', '"Surely it won\'t notice if I take—"\\n—Theria the Sly, last words', '"Thanks to my father, I know how to fight. He also showed me why I must."', '"The \'pinnacle\' of advancement is a concept that exists only in the narrow minds of those with no ambition."\\n—Yawgmoth', '"The Ancestor saved us for a purpose."', '"The Northern Beacon flared, and even before the drawbridge finished its descent, the knights charged out."\\n—*Legend of the Gilded Knights*', '"The artificer assured me that the vial is strong enough to contain the dragon\'s breath. I just need to make sure to throw it far enough."\\n—Kunh Mei, last words', '"The body has limits. The mind does not."', '"The colossal thing rumbled over the ridge, tree husks crumbling before it. The ones we were already fighting howled as it came, their muscles suddenly surging, and we knew it was time to flee."\\n—Llanach, Skyshroud ranger', '"The dim resort to violence, for which the nimble prepare."\\n—Leovold, emissary of Trest', '"The emergence of the Eldrazi isn\'t necessarily a bad thing, as long as you\'ve already lived a fulfilling and complete life without regrets."\\n—Javad Nasrin, Ondu relic hunter', '"The finest pawns are those with pawns of their own."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"The greatest honor is to feed Atarka."', '"The key to safely studying any sliver is to find out what provokes it, then absolutely never do that."\\n—Rukarumel, field journal', '"The land grows only where the kami will it."\\n—Dosan the Falling Leaf', '"The land has its own intentions, beyond the understanding of those who live on it."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"The most powerful dreams visit those who shelter in a dragon\'s skull."\\n—Chianul, Who Whispers Twice', '"The perfect assistant is one that\'s responsive, dextrous, and capable of reaching all the high shelves."\\n—Coruk, Esper artificer', '"The perfection of the lotus reminds me of my hopes for this world . . . and my failures. I will not rest until I\'ve atoned for them."\\n—Karn', '"The predator knows the true way of the world. Life is conflict. Only the strong survive."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"The raging gale fans the flames of righteous wrath."', '"The realm of the gods opens before me!"', '"The sad truth is that the whip of Erebos is long enough to wrap around all our throats."\\n—Perisophia the philosopher', '"The seas are vast, but the skies are even more so. Why be content with one kingdom when I can rule them both?"', '"The specimen seems to be broken."', '"The sun banishes darkness every morning. I too will rise with such assuredness."\\n—Huatli', '"The threads of magic that protect this place were woven by my will."', '"The time for subtlety is over, darling."', '"The trees keep our history better than any digital device."\\n—Satsuki, the Living Lore', '"The union of sea and sky makes a perfect cover."\\n—Talrand, sky summoner', '"The visions haunt me. I see the end of the world, brought on by the search for the Immortal Sun."\\n—Shaper Pashona', '"The voice calls me here, yet I see only bones. Is this more dragon trickery?"\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The walls of Argive were built by a peaceful dynastic union that has guarded us against war for fifteen centuries. The lesson is clear."', '"The way it shakes its hood is astonishingly irritating."\\n—Neena, outland scout', '"The wise learn from successes as well as mistakes."', '"There is no greater burden than choosing who to save."\\n—Kamahl, druid acolyte', '"There is no justice when some profit and others go without."', '"There\'s nothing quite as satisfying as delivering a good kick to the face."\\n—Adrasteia, Akroan captain', '"They may show up with the wrong thigh bone or mandible, but they always show up."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"This garden is where my grandmother had her first breakthrough on biomodular logarithmic theory!"\\n—Zimone, Quandrix mage-student', '"This is the source, the line unbroken since the calamity that brought such monsters to our shores."\\n—Hastric, Thunian scout', '"This is what glory looks like."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"This one fights like a leonin!"\\n—Jor Kadeen', '"Through even our darkest days, we must never cease creating. Each new invention brings value to the world, be it beauty, utility, or both."\\n—Rashmi, aether-seer', '"Through every verdant field, every bough that hangs heavy with fruit, Karametra shows her love."', '"Time is like the Luxa River—though it flows in one direction, it can be diverted."', '"Today will end with a feast," gloated the dragon. And what a feast it was.', '"Vine-wreathed, he nurtures life among the dead."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"We give the audience what they want."\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"We must rebuild Taj-Nar. Not for Raksha, not for the Vanished Ones, but for those who still remain."', '"We shall forever roam."\\n—Ayli, high priest of the Eternal Pilgrims', '"We travel to know the land—its sacred spirit, its perils and blessings."', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What is mana but possibility, an idea not yet given form?"\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"What weapon will you bear against one who\'s mastered them all?"', '"What\'s the big deal? All things will eventually cease to be, this one\'s just getting a head start."\\n—Edorin, the Timesmith', '"Whatever the Eldrazi\'s purpose is, it has nothing to do with something so insignificant as us."\\n—Nirthu, lone missionary', '"When establishing a new hive in hostile territory, slivers abandon all sense of individual self-preservation to ensure the queen\'s survival."\\n—Rukarumel, field journal', '"When gods become apathetic, the people will worship anyone who answers their pleas."\\n—Kiora', '"When the herd moves, so should you."\\n—Yon Basrel, Oran-Rief survivalist', '"Wherever the strong would harm the weak, I will be there."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Why should our fates be decided by pompous decrees from an empty throne? Fight with me and seize the reins of your own destiny!"\\n—Risona, leader of the Asari Uprisers', '"Witherbloom always has the home-field advantage."\\n—Dina, Witherbloom mage-student', '"Yavimaya is one being—one vastness of rippling leaves, one deepness of roots, and one chatter of animals—of which I am one part."', '"You burn. I\'ll pillage."', '"You\'ve begun to understand the hedrons\' true purpose," said Ugin. "The Eldrazi can be imprisoned."\\n"And how did that work out last time?" asked Jace.', '"Your own frailty is your undoing. I am merely the one to expose it."', '"Your superstitions and mumblings are useless chaff before my righteousness."', "*Strixhaven Star* food critic Aspen Van Gnoot's coverage of the fight would go on to win a student journalism award for outstanding war reporting.", 'A capable mage can tune its focus, refracting mana through each disk in turn to cast any spell they desire.', 'A captured elemental makes for a potent, albeit unstable, power source.', "A faerie's glee at her trove quickly fades to contentment, then to boredom, then to an urge to steal more.", 'A fiery scourge for both flesh and soul.', 'A figure is moved on a map, and the tide of war changes.', 'A flickering beacon of righteous corruption.', 'A force as voracious as time itself.', 'A golden helix streaked skyward from the Helvault. A thunderous explosion shattered the silver monolith and Avacyn emerged, free from her prison at last.', 'A good blacksmith will craft the weapon you ask for. A master will craft the weapon you dream of.', 'A hungry lair of flourishing rot.', 'A seething locus of reverent rage.', 'A single survivor can repopulate a devastated hive within a week.', 'A smoldering storm of chilling fire.', 'A void as cryptic as reality itself.', 'After lightning struck the cliffs, the ore became iron, the iron became steel, and the steel became greaves. The lightning never left.', 'All are welcome.', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'All sounds harmonize with the Worldsoul.', 'All that glitters is yours.', 'All the wonders of the natural world in one breathtaking microcosm.', 'All will be harvested.', 'An unwelcome light on a dark and foggy night.', 'Anarchy comes in many forms: social, individual, Gruul . . .', 'And still the titans were not sated.', 'Anyone who says love is the greatest gift of all has never received a ruby the size of their face.', 'Archmage attacks are little more than annoyances to Kalamax.', 'As Jhoira restored the *Weatherlight*, a mushroom growing in its hold unexpectedly became her first crew member.', "As eons passed, the rock wore away, revealing the rich colors at the mountain's heart.", "As the muscle cords of the creature twitched, Hanna saw an unsettling unanimity in the others' rippling flesh. She didn't know what it meant, but she urged Sisay to keep the ship at a safe distance.", "As the ritual neared its climax, the exultant cultists waited with bated breath, unaware of the looming consequences of the scroll's translation error.", "As the time streams grew more and more unstable, Dominaria's creatures struggled to adapt. The intense pressures led to many dead ends but also to lethal new forms that appeared as suddenly as the ashen rains.", 'As wild and untamed as the Roil from which it was born.', "At Feather's command, squadrons of battle angels swarmed out of the *Parhelion II*, unsheathing blades made of molten dawn.", 'At a certain point, the only thing a wizard wants for is time. And after that, nothing.', 'At the end of the show, she stands alone on a stage brilliant with blood.', 'Atarka goblins meet their demise as readily as their Temur counterparts did, but usually under big, winged shadows.', 'Attacking a kami is considered bad luck, so seasoned mages have developed techniques to usher them back to the spirit realm without violence.', "Automaton inspectors ensure that the Consulate's stringent standards for mass production are upheld.", "Bear the weight of so many spirits and you'll surrender civility and restraint to savagery and instinct.", 'Beauty appears in strange places for those with eyes to see it.', 'Beauty is in the eye of the exploder.', 'Because sometimes the greatest enemy is paperwork.', "Before being presented to its lord, each shaku is blessed by every hero of every region within that lord's domain.", 'Between matches, combatants practice to stay in peak mental and physical form.', 'Beware the generosity of demons.', 'Bred as living shields, these slivers have proven unruly—they know they cannot be caught.', 'By guild tradition, any puddle of multicolored light on the cobblestones can serve as neutral ground.', 'Cantankerous and territorial, sandwurms claim even the skies above their dunes.', 'Cast out of Garenbrig for his crimes, Ennor turned to fae magic to fashion the perfect weapon for his revenge.', 'Caught between life and death, between land and sea, between thought and oblivion.', "Centuries ago, one man's vengeance plunged the world into ice and darkness.", "Checking around every corner doesn't help if you forget to look up.", 'Creator of life, bringer of death.', 'Crippling fear precedes it. A foul stench accompanies it. Death follows in its wake.', "Critics were struck first by the elemental's surprising grace, and then by its fists.", 'Denied the peace of the Blessed Sleep, geists lash out at the living, and the cycle of anger and unrest continues unbroken.', "Dinner and politics don't mix.", 'Drink deep, and know the path to the heart of the wilds.', "Dust and memory are all that remain in Ulamog's wake.", 'Each Eldrazi ancient spawned a lineage of horrors in unfathomable shapes.', 'Each path ever charted by an Omenseeker is etched into her eyes.', 'Each scar on its hide is a badge of honor.', "Each scorpion's venom is unique, thwarting sanctuary healers' attempts to develop an antidote.", 'Each temple is a door to a horrible future.', 'Even a fragment of a powerstone contains within it not just energy, but space—vast dimensions trapped in fragile crystal.', 'Even after a false god tore the magic from Dominaria, power still radiated from the Mirari sword that slew her.', 'Even dragons fear its silken strands.', 'Even in their mountain fortresses, the Akroans have learned not to anger Thassa.', 'Even more than carrion, they crave the last words of the dying.', 'Even when the flesh grows cold, knowledge waits in the bones for a master to release it.', 'Every cry lifts her allies toward the thunder.', 'Every movement is a summons—even your screams.', 'Every storm has an eye.', 'Exhale, and let the winds carry your soul for all eternity.', 'Far from human eyes, birds flit between vivid blossoms in a hidden paradise.', 'Few escape the Underworld. Fewer still escape fate.', 'Few who encounter the strange, human-like grove leave once the lilting chorus of the dryads reaches their ears.', 'Fields of battle turn to fields of grain.', "For some of Ghirapur's aerowrights, building thopters is a byproduct of larger construction efforts.", 'For the Phyrexians, death is not an end, nor a one-time occurrence.', "For wisdom's sake, it was built high to gaze on all things. For glory's sake, it was built high as a testament of power. For strength's sake, it was built high to repel all attacks.", 'Forged by divine hands to wander mortal realms.', 'Forked tails rustled. Talons clicked. A lone sliver streaked overhead like jagged lightning, and the hive thundered.', 'From the cracks in the stone, she reads stories of the past. From the swirling vines, she glimpses visions of the future.', 'From the storm of hellfire, the angel emerged, smiling.', "Getting airborne with a kitesail is easy. It's everything afterward that takes focus, skill, and luck.", "Ghirapur's most celebrated inventors have been immortalized in clockwork.", 'Gideon and Liliana may not have seen eye to eye, but that did not stop them from fighting side by side.', 'Good dogs stay by your side until the end. Great dogs leave to bring back aid.', "Grand Warlord Radha's challengers are always defeated, but she rewards the most passionate with the Flame of Keld. After that, they burn for her.", 'Guarded by cartographers, disdained by warlords, coveted by adventurers.', 'Harpies are among the most detested creatures in all of Theros... and they thoroughly deserve it.', 'He had heard rumors of the cities—the constant noise, the stagnant air, the tainted water—and he had no wish to learn if they were true.', 'He makes his home on the tallest mountain in Sejiri, where the vista is as endless as his patience.', 'Heart, mind, soul—weapons all.', 'Her presence on the battlefield can transform an unruly mob into a disciplined army.', 'Her webs, spun from her own hair, reach from Nyx to the mortal world and even into the Underworld.', 'Herala sighed as the creature pulled itself from the smoldering pit, the ground boiling beneath its still-glowing feet. She had just plowed that field.', 'Hidetsugu held over a dozen oni in blood oath. At his touch, rocks scorched. At his word, cities burned.', "His enemies wondered if the lich king's brutal death and unnatural rebirth had been his plan all along.", 'His heart is pure. His world is not.', 'History is not delicately woven. It is hammered with fire.', 'Hobs bury their kin far from home. They believe the dry, open ground keeps hags from stealing the bones and gwyllions from stealing the spirits.', 'If bribery and intimidation fail, Marchesa turns to her favorite form of persuasion.', 'If it comes for you, die boldly or die swiftly—for die you will.', "In an attempt to restore pride to Shiv and to forge an undying legacy, Rorix traveled far to compete for glory in Otaria's Grand Coliseum.", "In his hunger for power and knowledge, Urza dug deep into Dominaria's ancient past.", 'In life, they were a motley crew: farmers, lords, cutpurses, priests. In death, they are united in singular, benevolent purpose.', 'In the end, the lights fade, the land withers, and only the dead and vile remain.', 'In their final moments, the demons gazed upon grace in its purest form.', 'In time, not even the fire monks could keep up with Chandra.', 'Infinite possibilities contained in a finite space.', 'Infinitely powerless.', 'It embodies all possible meanings of the word "infinite."', 'It evades Phyrexians by hiding in the spaces between seconds.', 'It fears no sword and leaves no bones behind.', 'It gathers against the coming storm.', 'It harmonizes with the essence of its master.', 'It is everything and nothing.', 'It is the forest beyond the horizon, the mountain waiting to be climbed, the new land across the endless sea.', 'It provides what every discerning mage requires—time to think.', 'It slithers through the senses, constricting consciousness and poisoning perceptions.', 'It started as a mere drop of water. The Magic Mirror crystallized it into much more.', 'It takes guts to be a trailblazer.', 'It took the banning of temporal manipulation at Tolaria West to teach its students the value of time.', 'It was built by the Witch of Lochmere. Most of the wishes it grants are its own.', "It's a small step from revel to bloodbath.", "It's difficult to outwit something that doesn't speak, strategize, or even think.", "It's in the nature of fire to grow.", 'Its call disrupts the delicate balance of the inner ear, disorienting intruders without direct confrontation.', 'Its collapse is like the lashing out of a long-dead civilization that resents being forgotten.', 'Its emotions run high. You should just run.', 'Its footsteps of today are the lakes of tomorrow.', 'Its graceful glide paints the ocean floor with strokes of luminescence.', 'Jund is a world as cruel as those who call it home. Their brutal struggles scar the land even as it carves them in its image, a vicious circle spiraling out of control.', "Keep looking up and you'll miss what's right in front of your face.", 'Klothys set out to mend the destiny of Theros, her fury guiding every stitch.', "Legend speaks of the lost coastal polis of Olantin, whose inhabitants' hubris enraged the sun god Heliod.", 'Liliana insisted on coming to Amonkhet to confront one of the two remaining demons to whom she is bound.', "Linger on death's door and risk being invited in.", 'Lives taken are lives not easily forgotten.', 'Living proof that friendship and loyalty transcend language.', "Lomelda had spent four semesters on the waitlist for Kasmina's Advanced Polymorphological Theory seminar. She was determined not to miss a word.", "Lost at sea doesn't have to mean lost forever.", "Lost to time is the artificer's art of trapping light from a distant star in a ring of purest gold.", "Mages and warriors recruited from across Kylem display their skills at Valor's Reach.", 'Many sigils, one purpose.', 'Martyred for worshipping her ancestors, she now walks among them.', "Matic had only taken the ring to appease his grandmother when she'd pressed it insistently into his palm. As the rats scurried away from its light, he understood her urgency.", "Mirrodin's heart beats with Phyrexian oil.", 'Mogglings have been known to play ball with hibernating slivers, completely unaware of their true nature.', 'More than heat and the strength of his arm, it was his faith that gave the blade its unyielding edge.', 'Most mirrors show your reflection. Others show your potential.', 'Most see krakens as wantonly violent, failing to notice their meticulous attention to detail when dismantling a vessel.', 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', "Nevinyrral's final act of spite was to make sure all of his magic was destroyed along with him.", 'Newborn slivers will sometimes wrap themselves playfully around a human\'s finger. They grow out of the "playful" part.', 'No thought but hunger. No strategy but destruction.', 'Not all storms come from the sky.', "Not even the tallest tree stands a chance against the underside of a dinosaur's foot.", 'Nothing shatters a peaceful life like newfound riches.', 'On Naya, ambition and treachery are scarce, hunted nearly to extinction by the awe owed to terrestrial gods.', 'On Otaria, peace and harmony are rare. Places that provide both are cherished.', 'On the continent of Tazeem, rushing waters plunge through narrow canyons into mist-cloaked lakes.', 'On the volcanic continent of Akoum, bizarre vegetation clusters around gas vents, and jagged mountain peaks rise high into the air.', 'Once a center for knowledge, Sea Gate now serves as a reminder of what was lost.', 'Once guarded by the Knights of the Reliquary, the tower stands now protected only by its own remoteness, its dusty treasures open to plunder by anyone.', 'Once the last few slivers the Riptide Project controlled were dead, there was nothing to keep the island from being completely overrun.', "One half-written novel, a year's worth of lecture notes, and several grocery lists later, Shiori began to wonder if she'd hacked the wrong terminal.", 'One quiet word sets off the stampede.', 'Only the Eldrazi mind thinks in the warped paths required to open the hedrons and tap the power within.', "Oona's song is like a twisted dinner chime. All the faeries return home, but it is Oona who feasts—on the stolen dreams and rumors they serve her.", 'Other Phyrexians have nightmares about the gargantua.', 'Otrimi was disappointed at how quickly its new friend got tired and stopped playing.', 'Panic spread like wildfire as the demons of Immersturm poured into Bretagard, slaughtering as they came.', 'Pharika has written her secrets on its bones so that only the worthy may discover them.', "Phenax, god of deception, offered the soldiers protection from every poison on Theros. He saw no need to mention that Pharika's poisons were drawn from Nyx.", "Raksha's sudden departure split the leonin into two prides. The fight for survival reunited them.", 'Remote but always watching, the soaring city of Otawara moves over Kamigawa with a purpose that few understand.', 'Rumors float through the city like crows, alighting on citizens seemingly at random.', 'Rumors quickly spread among thieves about a labyrinth without walls and a prize beyond all measures of worth.', 'Scholars say that arbiters exist on every world, created by an unknown hand to enforce justice.', 'She cares little for leaders or loyalties, so long as the battle rages on.', 'She chooses her riders carefully and bears them to glory in battle after battle.', 'She formed a friendship with several playful spirits, and soon "the pack" was known as the source of much mischief in Eiganjo.', "She remembers every word spoken, from the hero's oath to the baby's cry.", 'She talks using riddles her disciples alone can unravel.', 'Silent as a snowdrift. Inexorable as an avalanche.', 'Slivers will swiftly adapt to fill any evolutionary niche, even if that niche is "earthshaking apex predator."', 'Some blades seek their own wielders.', 'Some find inspiration in their swords. Others find it in their leaders.', 'Some spells sing a quiet tune. Others roar.', 'Some timelines forever fray, branch, and intermingle. Others end abruptly.', 'Some will sacrifice everything for but a taste of power.', "Sometimes it's useful to take a break from existence.", 'Sometimes the strongest weapon you can hold in your hand is another hand.', 'Squee had been disemboweled many times before, but never by something so stunningly beautiful.', "Taborax's cultists are the latest in a long history of beings who have desired to see Zendikar torn to pieces.", 'Tahngarth relished the chance to bloody his blades on those who had ravaged his home.', 'Thallids nurture saprolings, entertain them, and eat them.', 'That which endures, survives.', 'The Auriok see the artificer as a conduit, beckoning new creations into the world.', 'The Eldrazi hunger without limit and consume without pause.', 'The Hold, an illegal research facility in a derelict merchant ship, became a wellspring of renegade intelligence.', 'The Izzet signet is redesigned often, each time becoming closer to a vanity portrait of Niv-Mizzet.', 'The Izzet specialize in unnatural disaster.', "The Keldons used the toxic vents in the cracked earth to bolster their home's defenses.", 'The Law of Givesies Backsies is respected by every noble pursuer of shiny things.', "The Spitfire Bastion bristles with cannons claimed from every ship she's conquered.", "The arrival of spring's first flowers is a sacred occasion to Karametra's acolytes, who fill the Setessan woods with song in celebration.", 'The best presents are impossible to regift.', 'The best recipes start with reliable cookware.', 'The best swords are forged with dragonfire.', "The blade glows only for Zendikar's chosen.", "The city mourned Niv-Mizzet's death, but he left behind the components for his rebirth.", "The continent of Bala Ged was ravaged by massive Eldrazi of Ulamog's lineage, its lush jungles and cascading rivers reduced to dust.", 'The continent of Guul Draz is a geothermal swampland reeking of heat and decay.', 'The continent of Murasa lies beneath a blanket of dense vegetation, its enormous branches tangled so thickly that some inhabitants never see the ground.', 'The continent of Ondu is a vast plateau crisscrossed by deep trenches and meandering rivers.', "The dead know lessons the living haven't learned.", 'The dense jungle surrenders to a lush and lavish expanse. At its center uncoil the spires of Qarsi Palace.', 'The desert is a voracious beast, devouring both flesh and stone.', 'The directors of the Riptide Project wanted instant results on the sliver experiments. They got their wish.', "The distinction of bearing the gods' banner is nothing compared to the glory of being closer to Nyx.", 'The earth walks, strongest of all.', 'The emotional echoes of dryad gatherings attract lost souls.', 'The first searchlights were given as gifts, symbols of cooperation, to the emissaries present at the signing of the Guildpact.', 'The gate of every kithkin doun is a cunning trap, intended to spill visitors into an oubliette from which there is no escape.', 'The gods known to the merfolk as Ula, Emeria, and Cosi were nothing more than false memories of a monstrous trinity: the Eldrazi titans Ulamog, Emrakul, and Kozilek.', 'The great library in the Museum of Old Capenna has a million volumes on display—and miles of passages hidden behind them.', 'The hammer strikes. The Flame awakens.', 'The hive knows no fear or mercy, only hunger.', 'The kami permit few mortals to dwell in Jukai Forest, but the clever, playful tanuki are welcomed as friends and guardians.', 'The kor send their thopter kites to see if the land is in a welcoming mood.', 'The letter unfolded, inviting the twins to Strixhaven. Will saw a chance for arcane study. Rowan saw a chance for power.', 'The litany of the infernal on his flesh pulses to the beating of his dark heart.', 'The loudest and most heartfelt cheers come from the cheap seats.', "The luckiest acolytes were those who didn't survive long enough to see the archfiend's return.", 'The maze-like design embodies the core of Azorius law —strict structure designed to test wills and stall change.', 'The militia formed up in the central plaza awaiting the onslaught, but the giants never quite made it.', 'The mouth must be pried open before rigor mortis sets in. Otherwise the returning soul can find no ingress.', 'The myr are like the Glimmervoid: blank canvases on which to build grand creations.', 'The only thing more ill-tempered than a griffin in a web is the spider that must subdue it.', "The orcs believe Sek'Kuar still lives in the Karplusan Mountains, gathering his dead army, intent on revenge.", 'The path of a goblin shaman is a journey through a thousand ways of hurting people.', 'The province of Jingzhou was the fulcrum of the three kingdoms. At separate times it was coveted and controlled by the Wu, the Shu, and the Wei.', 'The pyromancer summoned up her mightiest onslaught of fire and rage. Jace feigned interest.', 'The rifted multiverse became a sea of conflicting realities, each peopled by possible versions of every living being.', 'The sky takes flight and the earth trembles.', 'The smallest seed of regret can bloom into redemption.', 'The soldiers were hopelessly outmatched, having brought only swords, ballistas, fire, spellcraft, and several large cannons to the battle.', 'The spirit dragon Ugin arranged the hedrons of Zendikar to direct leylines of energy. To disrupt one is to unleash devastation and chaos.', 'The venom softens tissue and liquefies internal organs, allowing the slivers to feed freely without wasting time chewing.', 'Their pearlescent scales are highly sought after by those who lack the instincts for self-preservation.', 'There is a sanctuary that reveals itself only to those graced by the *eludha*—the mystical connection between bonder and monster.', 'There is no such thing as surprising a sliver.', 'They hunt on pure instinct, driven by the will of the hive mind with no time wasted on independent thought.', 'Those who crave power for selfish ends find that it always floats just beyond their fingertips, forever maddeningly out of reach.', 'Those who die as heroes are permitted to dwell in Ilysia, a protected realm of the Underworld as tranquil and vibrant as the rest is bleak.', 'Those who forget the horrors of the past are doomed to re-meet them.', 'Those who love the woods only wish to spread its majesty.', 'Those with knowledge are wise to listen to those with imagination.', 'Though Volrath is long dead, the slivers have become everything he wanted them to be: mindless instruments of destruction and despair.', "To get to Valor's Reach, competitors must first make a name for themselves in the smaller arenas.", 'To the Rakdos, screams of delight and screams of terror are one and the same.', 'To the Zendikari, an apocalypse. To the Eldrazi, a day like any other.', 'To understand Ravnica, one must first understand how each guild contributes to its stability.', 'Travelers bathe in the falls to wash away curses from the pucas who lurk nearby.', "Traveling across the desert alone, you might assume you'd see them coming, but that would be your third mistake.", 'Unable to touch items of value, he goes forth to steal secrets instead.', 'Unburdened from mortality, archaics wander the Vastlands seeking knowledge only they can comprehend.', 'Urza studied the creations of the Thran not simply to learn from them, but to surpass them.', 'Urza threw himself into his research, pushing the boundaries of both possibility and morality.', "Urza's metathran children were conceived, birthed, and nurtured by an integrated system of machines.", 'Warm enough to incubate eggs or incinerate those who would eat them.', "Warning to those who scale the cliffs without paying tribute: It's a long way down.", "Were she not a judge, she'd win the division herself.", 'When Asha left Bant, she ensured that the world would have protection and order in her absence.', "When Belzenlok's lieutenant Yar-Kul grew too ambitious, the Demonlord transformed him into a maggot. The frog that ate the maggot grew and grew, until a ravenous spirit burst from its body.", 'When Lorthos emerges from his deepwater realm, the tides bow to his will and the coastline cowers in his presence.', 'When a species becomes so dominant that no other can compete, evolution gets creative.', 'When asked how many paths reach enlightenment, the monk kicked a heap of sand. "Count," he smiled, "and then find more grains."', 'When defeat is near and guidance is scarce, all eyes look in one direction.', 'When it wriggled closer to a thrum of slivers, their talons hardened and glinted in the sun. One took a playful swipe at a tree trunk, and its new blade cut clean through.', 'When the last scrap of flesh is scoured away, the Curse of Wandering ends. Then the dead may sleep.', 'When the price of your sins comes due, the Church of Deals is there to collect.', "When they're done pummeling each other, the fighters relax companionably in the springs, warming their sore muscles.", 'Where victors are commemorated and moments of glory immortalized.', 'Wherever Yanggu goes, Mowu follows—sometimes at his side, sometimes obscuring him from view entirely.', 'Whether hunter or hunted, Kathril chooses when it is seen.', 'While Kaya is guildmaster, Teysa waits patiently at the center of the Orzhov web of power.', 'Wildflowers here bloom not with the season but with the ebb and flow of magic.', 'With a roar, the forest came alive.', 'Within weeks, more slivers nested in Otaria than ever existed on Rath.', "You don't want to know how she got that name.", "Zombies work best when they're fed appropriately, so it's prudent to let them eat on the job."]
